        </svg>
        WhatsApp Now
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Quick Stats Section -->
<section style="padding:4rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e00;">
  <div class="container">
    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:1px;background:#000000;">
      <div style="background:#000;padding:2rem;text-align:center;">
        <div style="font-size:2rem;font-weight:200;color:#e00;margin-bottom:0.5rem;">FREE</div>
        <div style="font-size:0.7rem;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#FFFFFF;">Initial Consultation</div>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#000;padding:2rem;text-align:center;">
        <div style="font-size:2rem;font-weight:200;color:#e00;margin-bottom:0.5rem;">10-25%</div>
        <div style="font-size:0.7rem;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#FFFFFF;">Cost Reduction Potential</div>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#000;padding:2rem;text-align:center;">
        <div style="font-size:2rem;font-weight:200;color:#e00;margin-bottom:0.5rem;">500+</div>
        <div style="font-size:0.7rem;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#FFFFFF;">Brands Advised</div>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#000;padding:2rem;text-align:center;">
        <div style="font-size:2rem;font-weight:200;color:#e00;margin-bottom:0.5rem;">26+</div>
        <div style="font-size:0.7rem;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#FFFFFF;">Years Experience</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Who Needs Fashion Consulting Section -->
<section style="padding:5rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e00;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header" style="margin-bottom:3rem;">
      <span class="section-label">Who We Help</span>
      <div class="accent-line"></div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.4rem);font-weight:300;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1rem;">Who Needs Fashion Consulting</h2>
    </div>
    
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;">
      Fashion consulting is valuable for new fashion brands launching their first collection and navigating manufacturing for the first time. We help you understand production processes, make informed decisions, and avoid costly mistakes that first-time brands commonly make.
    </p>
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1rem;">
      Established brands also benefit from consulting when expanding into new categories, entering new markets, or experiencing quality and cost issues with current manufacturers. We provide the manufacturing expertise that fashion designers and business owners often lack in-house.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Brand Strategy Consultation Section -->
<section style="padding:5rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e00;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header" style="margin-bottom:3rem;">
      <span class="section-label">Strategic Guidance</span>
      <div class="accent-line"></div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.4rem);font-weight:300;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1rem;">Brand Strategy Consultation</h2>
    </div>
    
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;">
      Brand strategy consultation helps define your manufacturing approach based on your brand identity, target market, and business goals. We assess whether your product line aligns with suitable manufacturing models, recommend appropriate quality levels and certifications, and help position your brand competitively through strategic production choices.
    </p>
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1rem;">
      We evaluate your brand positioning against manufacturing realities | ensuring your price point, quality expectations, and production timelines are achievable. This strategic alignment prevents disappointment and ensures sustainable growth.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Manufacturing Strategy Section -->
<section style="padding:5rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e00;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header" style="margin-bottom:3rem;">
      <span class="section-label">Production Models</span>
      <div class="accent-line"></div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.4rem);font-weight:300;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1rem;">Manufacturing Strategy: OEM vs ODM vs CMT</h2>
    </div>
    
    <h3 style="font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:400;color:#e00;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">OEM (Original Equipment Manufacturer)</h3>
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.92rem;margin-bottom:2rem;">
      We make garments using your designs and tech pack. You own all intellectual property. Best for brands with established design capabilities and clear product specifications. Higher MOQs but full control over design.
    </p>

    <h3 style="font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:400;color:#e00;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">ODM (Original Design Manufacturer)</h3>
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.92rem;margin-bottom:2rem;">
      We design the garment for you and you put your brand on it. We own the design IP but grant exclusive usage rights. Best for brands needing design assistance or faster time-to-market. Lower MOQs but less design control.
    </p>

    <h3 style="font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:400;color:#e00;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">CMT (Cut, Make, Trim)</h3>
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.92rem;">
      You provide all materials and we only handle cutting, sewing, and finishing. Best for brands with established material supply chains or proprietary fabrics. Lowest manufacturing cost but highest coordination burden on your side.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Cost Optimization Section -->
<section style="padding:5rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e00;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header" style="margin-bottom:3rem;">
      <span class="section-label">Cost Management</span>
      <div class="accent-line"></div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.4rem);font-weight:300;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1rem;">Cost Optimization Advice</h2>
    </div>
    
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;">
      We analyze your product specifications and suggest cost-saving alternatives that maintain quality. Cost optimization can reduce FOB pricing by 10-25% without compromising garment integrity or brand perception.
    </p>
    <ul style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.9;list-style:none;padding:0;margin:1.5rem 0;max-width:800px;">
      <li style="margin-bottom:0.75rem;padding-left:1.5rem;position:relative;">
        <span style="color:#e00;position:absolute;left:0;">✓</span>
        Recommending alternative fabrics with similar performance
      </li>
      <li style="margin-bottom:0.75rem;padding-left:1.5rem;position:relative;">
        <span style="color:#e00;position:absolute;left:0;">✓</span>
        Simplifying construction where possible without affecting aesthetics
      </li>
      <li style="margin-bottom:0.75rem;padding-left:1.5rem;position:relative;">
        <span style="color:#e00;position:absolute;left:0;">✓</span>
        Consolidating colors to reduce dyeing setup costs
      </li>
      <li style="margin-bottom:0.75rem;padding-left:1.5rem;position:relative;">
        <span style="color:#e00;position:absolute;left:0;">✓</span>
        Optimizing size runs for better fabric utilization
      </li>
      <li style="padding-left:1.5rem;position:relative;">
        <span style="color:#e00;position:absolute;left:0;">✓</span>
        Identifying unnecessary trims or packaging
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- MOQ Planning Section -->
<section style="padding:5rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e00;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header" style="margin-bottom:3rem;">
      <span class="section-label">Order Planning</span>
      <div class="accent-line"></div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.4rem);font-weight:300;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1rem;">MOQ Planning</h2>
    </div>
    
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;">
      MOQ planning ensures your order sizes align with manufacturer minimums while meeting your business needs. We help you determine optimal order quantities, plan size and color breakdowns to meet MOQs efficiently, and schedule production to consolidate orders.
    </p>
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1rem;">
      Proper MOQ planning prevents overstocking, reduces unit costs through efficient ordering, and ensures smooth production flow. We teach you how to work within manufacturer constraints while protecting your cash flow and inventory management.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Timeline and Seasonal Planning Section -->
<section style="padding:5rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e00;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header" style="margin-bottom:3rem;">
      <span class="section-label">Production Scheduling</span>
      <div class="accent-line"></div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.4rem);font-weight:300;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1rem;">Timeline and Seasonal Planning</h2>
    </div>
    
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;">
      Fashion production operates on seasonal cycles. We help you plan production timelines aligned with fashion seasons, factoring in development time, material sourcing lead times, production duration, and shipping.
    </p>
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1rem;">
      We create production calendars that ensure your collection arrives in time for launch, with buffer time for unexpected delays. Proper planning prevents missed seasons, cash flow issues, and rushed production that compromises quality.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- FAQ Section -->
<section style="padding:5rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e00;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header" style="margin-bottom:3rem;">
      <span class="section-label">Common Questions</span>
      <div class="accent-line"></div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.4rem);font-weight:300;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1rem;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    </div>
    
    <div style="max-width:800px;">
      <div style="border-bottom:1px solid #e00;padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Who needs fashion consulting service?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">Fashion consulting is valuable for new fashion brands launching their first collection, established brands expanding into new categories or markets, brands experiencing quality or cost issues with current manufacturers, and brands planning to scale production. We provide the manufacturing expertise that fashion designers and business owners often lack.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="border-bottom:1px solid #e00;padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">What does brand strategy consultation cover?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">Brand strategy consultation helps define your manufacturing approach based on your brand identity, target market, and business goals. We assess whether your product line aligns with suitable manufacturing models, recommend appropriate quality levels and certifications, and help position your brand competitively through strategic production choices.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="border-bottom:1px solid #e00;padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">What is the difference between OEM, ODM, and CMT?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">OEM (Original Equipment Manufacturer) means we make garments using your designs and tech pack. You own the IP. ODM (Original Design Manufacturer) means we design the garment for you and you put your brand on it. We own the design IP. CMT (Cut, Make, Trim) means you provide all materials and we only handle cutting, sewing, and finishing. Each model has different cost structures, MOQs, and IP considerations.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="border-bottom:1px solid #e00;padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">How can you help with cost optimization?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">We analyze your product specifications and suggest cost-saving alternatives that maintain quality. This includes recommending alternative fabrics with similar performance, simplifying construction where possible, consolidating colors to reduce dyeing costs, optimizing size runs for better fabric utilization, and identifying unnecessary trims or packaging. Cost optimization can reduce FOB pricing by 10-25% without compromising quality.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="border-bottom:1px solid #e00;padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">What is MOQ planning and why does it matter?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">MOQ planning ensures your order sizes align with manufacturer minimums while meeting your business needs. We help you determine optimal order quantities, plan size and color breakdowns to meet MOQs efficiently, and schedule production to consolidate orders. Proper MOQ planning prevents overstocking, reduces unit costs, and ensures smooth production flow.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">How does timeline and seasonal planning work?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">Fashion production operates on seasonal cycles. We help you plan production timelines aligned with fashion seasons, factor in development time, material sourcing lead times, production duration, and shipping. We create production calendars that ensure your collection arrives in time for launch, with buffer time for unexpected delays. Proper planning prevents missed seasons and cash flow issues.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- CTA Section -->
<section style="padding:5rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e00;">
  <div class="container">
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;">
      Need strategic guidance for your fashion brand's manufacturing decisions? <a href="/contact" style="color:#e00;text-decoration:underline;">Contact SDF Clothing here</a> for a free initial consultation. We'll review your brand situation, production challenges, and goals | and provide actionable recommendations. No obligation.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Internal Link Section -->
<section style="padding:5rem 0;">
  <div class="container">
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;">
      For hands-on development support, read our <a href="/garment-development-service" style="color:#e00;text-decoration:underline;">garment development service guide</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>


    
